{"id": "EUVD-2026-96547", "enisaUuid": "a6673ab8-ce2b-377c-973f-0b2cb80b379c", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains an insecure direct object reference vulnerability that allows authenticated users to delete other users' AI voice records by supplying an arbitrary userId to DELETE /airag/voice/deleteVoiceRecord. Attackers can obtain record ids from the unchecked GET /airag/voice/listByUser endpoint and delete victims' text-to-speech history entries stored in Redis, one per request.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T02:29:08", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_airag_voice_record_delete.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-boot-module/jeecg-boot-module-airag/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/airag/voice/controller/VoiceController.java#L83-L90", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-idor-via-deletevoicerecord-userid-parameter"], "aliases": ["GHSA-c23h-4967-rhxw", "CVE-2026-108608"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "360daa33-f4c0-3837-b6cb-6ba7ce31b900", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8fa5910f-aa9b-3afd-93ce-dcdb23ac2db3", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}